    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0190" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg120"/>

                <head>No. 62.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Logan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 3,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge your No. 122, of the
                    15th of August last, in regard to the alleged joint action of France, England,
                    Germany and <pb facs="0191" n="121" xml:id="pg121"/> Italy in the affairs of the
                    Pacific coast of South America, and to approve your refusal to be approached in
                    the matter. Beyond your dispatch the Department as yet has no information on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
